# Imports: separate type imports

Types must always be imported with a dedicated `import type { … }` statement. Never mix types and values in the same import (no inline `type` modifiers).

## Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — types and values in separate imports
import type { AppError, Result } from './result';
import { ERROR_CODE, fromPb, panic } from './result';

import type { AppUser } from '#lib/auth/user.js';
import { parseAppUser } from '#lib/auth/user.js';
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — inline `type` in a value import
import { type AppError, ERROR_CODE, fromPb, panic } from './result';
import { type AppUser, parseAppUser } from '#lib/auth/user.js';
import { ok, type Result, type ResultAsync } from 'neverthrow';
```

## Do not

- Use `import { type X, y }` or `import { x, type Y }`
- Prefer a single mixed import over two separate ones for the same module
